<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The analysis of a) inversion timestep, b) cross-attention replacement, and c) the reward during the training of the policy model <math id="S4.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Across Training Episodes.</span>
We plot the reward of AutoEdit on DDPM-Inversion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> over the first 3000 training episodes. The results are shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F4.sf3" title="In Figure 4 ‣ 4.3 AutoEdit Improves the Performance over Other Methods ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ AutoEdit: Automatic Hyperparameter Tuning for Image Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(c)</span></a>, where episode 0 corresponds to the <span id="S4.SS3.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase-1</span> model <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We observed a consistent increase in reward during PPO training up to episode 2500, after which it slightly declined at episode 3000. Based on this trend, we limit training to the first 2500 episodes (approximately 15 epochs).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

